.TH MAKE-TEST.SH 1 "2026-09-24" "pg_claster_creator" "Workspace tools"
.SH NAME
make-test.sh \- run test helpers on one local Linux host or WSL distribution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash tools/make-test.sh
.RB [ --local ]
.RB [ --repo " DIR"]
.RB [ --package " NAME"]
.RB [ --port " PORT"]
.RB [ --output-dir " DIR"]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Workspace-only launcher for TEST.md. No test starts without answering y/Y to
the first default-No prompt. A second default-No prompt separately authorizes
deleting all original clusters and reinstalling PostgreSQL/Tantor/common packages.
An installed server takes precedence. If it has any original registered cluster,
server/common reinstallation and dependency-removal tests are skipped. Original
cluster deletion still requires the second confirmation. If no server is installed,
provision by product priority (SE/Enterprise, BE, Free/PostgreSQL; newest major
within each tier). The existing claster-creator package/config remain prerequisites.
Declining the second runs isolated helpers and live SQL singl/struct-dirs on
a private unregistered test_<random 1..9> PostgreSQL server with a free port.
Only its private Unix socket is enabled. A test-local registry adapter exercises
SQL functions without changing /etc/postgresql. Original clusters and packages
are compared before/after. Destructive variants are skipped, not failures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --local
Use the current Linux machine; requires root after confirmation. Default target.
.TP
.BI --repo " DIR"
Source path visible on the target; defaults to the launcher's project directory.
.TP
.BI --package " NAME"
Select an installed server for safe SQL; assert the detected server for destructive
testing, which supports only one initial server installation.
.TP
.BI --port " PORT"
Destructive QA base port, 60100 through 60800 in steps of 100. By default,
randomly reserve an available 100-port range. Parallel WSL runs must share
the evidence root: atomic reservations prevent overlapping test ranges.
On interruption, retain the reservation until child processes have been checked.
Safe SQL selects a free port automatically.
.TP
.BI --output-dir " DIR"
Per-release evidence root on the target. Default: documented WSL backup path,
or /tmp/pg_claster_creator/TEST-X.Y.Z on native Linux. An explicit --output-dir
overrides this default. Copy results before temporary-directory cleanup/reboot.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage without changes.
.SH WINDOWS WRAPPER
Run tools\\make-test.cmd --wsl DISTRO from Windows CMD or PowerShell.
The wrapper computes /mnt/<lowercase drive>/.../tools/make-test.sh from its
own directory and invokes it as root with --local. Both confirmations remain.
Requires Windows PowerShell and WSL; UNC paths and nonstandard automount roots
are unsupported. Extra options require direct invocation of .sh inside WSL.
The Bash runner rejects --wsl and positional distribution names.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Inherited PGCC_* and CLASTER_FORCE_* settings are cleared before testing.
The launcher supplies internal PGCC_TEST_REPO/RELEASE/RUN/OUTPUT/HOST to helpers.
.SH RESULTS
Both modes exercise tools/sql-tests on a private temporary server: six nested
scripts in relative-path order, then root 00.sql separately as the PASS/FAIL oracle.
See sql-tree-result.log; the destructive mode names this stage sql-struct-dirs.
Creates <output-dir>/<host>/<run-id>/TEST-X.Y.Z-journal.md for each run.
The saved log directory is printed at exit, on both success and failure,
once the directory has been created.
Launcher output is stored in launcher/<stage>.log, separate from helper logs.
Stage exit codes and error paths are printed on the console.
Aligned start/finish lines show timestamps, PASS/FAIL and elapsed M:SS.mmm.
Stages lasting longer than five seconds show elapsed M:SS, updated every
second on one terminal line (separate lines when output is redirected).
After helpers/audits finish, .log files larger than 100 KiB (102400 bytes)
are compressed to .log.gz, including failed runs. Append .gz to journal log
paths when applicable. Existing archives are never overwritten; symlinks are skipped.
Existing project-root journals are neither modified nor used as a startup guard. Automated
helper success is not full plan coverage; unverified variants remain untested.
No automatic passed suffix. A host lock prevents concurrent launcher runs.
Temporary source copies are retained on failure for recovery. No --yes bypass.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: completed automated chain or cancellation; 1: test/cleanup failure;
2: invalid arguments/prerequisites; 130/143: interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
TEST.md, create-claster.sh(1), create-claster-deb.sh(1)
